[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/testcontainers/testcontainers-java/issues/comments/205043330","html_url":"https://github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-java/issues/118#issuecomment-205043330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/testcontainers/testcontainers-java/issues/118","id":205043330,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIwNTA0MzMzMA==","user":{"login":"rnorth","id":132175,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjE3NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth","html_url":"https://github.com/rnorth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rnorth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-04-03T19:52:10Z","updated_at":"2016-04-03T19:52:10Z","body":"Thanks! :smile: \n\nUnfortunately there's no way to stop that failure from happening right now, though you could change logback filters to suppress the message for the appender named `🐳 [richnorth/ambassador:latest]`. Sorry that this is clunky at the moment.\n\nThis should clearly be improved, though, and the behaviour that's causing the message should be removed. As-is, the library attempts to start an 'ambassador container' (one that exposes ports that would otherwise only be accessible through container links) - but does so straight away after starting the docker compose container. Since the docker compose container takes some time to create 